# This file keeps the chromiumprofile/ directory tracked by git while the
# directory itself stays empty by default.
#
# To ship a pre-configured Chrome profile with the Docker image:
#   1. Copy your Chrome profile folder contents here:
#        cp -r ~/Desktop/chromiumprofile/* ./chromiumprofile/
#   2. Build normally:
#        ./upload             # multi-arch push to Docker Hub
#        docker compose build # local only
#
# The Dockerfile copies everything in this folder to /app/chromiumprofile/
# inside the image, and CHROME_USER_DATA_DIR defaults to that path.
#
# If this folder is empty (no profile copied), Chrome creates a fresh profile
# at /app/chromiumprofile/ on first launch — still persistent within the
# container lifetime.
#
# For cross-restart persistence without baking the profile in, mount a volume:
#   docker run -v ./chromiumprofile:/app/chromiumprofile ...
